%% Attention Sink — one cycle, end to end.
%% Source of truth for the ordering; the rendered SVG at
%% docs/showcase/assets/readme/cycle-sequence.svg is laid out by
%% scripts/build_showcase_diagrams.py so it stays legible at README width.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SCHED as EventBridge Scheduler
    participant CYCLE as Run-Cycle Lambda
    participant BR as Amazon Bedrock
    participant POL as Policy engine
    participant DDB as Amazon DynamoDB
    participant BUS as Amazon EventBridge
    participant ANA as Analysis Lambda
    participant API as Public read API
    participant WEB as Exhibition frontend

    SCHED->>CYCLE: invoke — rate(2 minutes), one cycle
    CYCLE->>DDB: load six committed arm states and the next stimulus
    CYCLE->>BR: six writer calls: same stimulus, same prompt, no arm name
    BR->>CYCLE: journal entry, candidate memory, claimed citations
    CYCLE->>POL: validate citations against the active set
    POL->>BR: Dreamer only — one extra call to write the summary
    POL->>CYCLE: evict or compress until the arm fits 208 tokens
    CYCLE->>DDB: TransactWriteItems — all six snapshots, or none
    CYCLE->>BUS: emit cycle-completed
    BUS->>ANA: rule fires
    ANA->>DDB: recall, drift, echo, contradiction — written back
    WEB->>API: visitor opens a cycle
    API->>DDB: read committed state only; a cycle in flight is invisible

    Note over CYCLE,DDB: Steps 1-8 are the experiment. Everything after<br/>step 8 reads what step 8 committed and can never change it.
